{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:1", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "1"}, "paraphrase": "The opening names: the auspicious Mother, the great Queen, the empress seated on the lion-throne; she who arose from the fire-altar of consciousness and is intent on accomplishing the gods' purpose.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "sound"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "world-fate"], "original": {"text": "śrīmātā śrīmahārājñī śrīmatsiṃhāsaneśvarī / cidagnikuṇḍasambhūtā devakāryasamudyatā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "terms": ["trm:lalita", "trm:amba"], "concepts": ["cpt:lalita-as-brahman"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:112", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "112"}, "paraphrase": "Her form is self-awareness (vimarśa); she is the vidyā, and mother of the world beginning with space.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:prakasa-vimarsa"], "terms": ["trm:vimarsa"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:117-118", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "117-118"}, "paraphrase": "She is the knowledge of the self (ātmavidyā), the great knowledge (mahāvidyā), Śrīvidyā, served by Kāma; the sixteen-syllable vidyā, three-peaked (trikūṭā), Kāmakoṭikā.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "knowledge"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:srividya-mantra-structure"], "terms": ["trm:srividya", "trm:sodasi", "trm:kuta"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:124-125", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "124-125"}, "paraphrase": "She is the mother of countless crores of universes and of divine form; she grants the state of isolation-liberation (kaivalya); she is Tripurā, worshipped by the three worlds, the three forms (trimūrti), the ruler of the gods.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation", "world-fate"], "concepts": ["cpt:tripura-triads"], "terms": ["trm:tripura", "trm:kaivalya"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:138", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "138"}, "paraphrase": "She is free of all limiting adjuncts, devoted to Sadāśiva, sovereign of the tradition (sampradāyeśvarī), and of the form of the circle of gurus (gurumaṇḍala).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-oghas"], "terms": ["trm:guru-mandala", "trm:sampradaya"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:140", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "140"}, "paraphrase": "She is independent, the ruler of all tantras, of the form of Dakṣiṇāmūrti, worshipped by Sanaka and the others, the giver of the knowledge of Śiva.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "ultimate"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:141-142", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "141-142"}, "paraphrase": "She delights in the recitation of her names; she is the substratum of the illusory world (mithyā-jagad-adhiṣṭhānā), the giver of liberation and liberation itself.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "absolute", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "karma-liberation", "practice"], "original": {"text": "nāmapārāyaṇaprītā nandividyā naṭeśvarī / mithyājagadadhiṣṭhānā muktidā muktirūpiṇī", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:maya-as-sakti"], "practices": ["prc:lalita-sahasranama-parayana"], "disputes": ["dsp:maya-sakti-or-avidya"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:156", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "156"}, "paraphrase": "She is of the form of the fifty seats (pīṭha); unfettered, dwelling apart, the mother of heroes, the source of space.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "ritual"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["sound-language", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:matrka-and-fifty-pithas"], "terms": ["trm:pitha", "trm:matrka"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:162", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "162"}, "paraphrase": "She is to be worshipped by those turned inward and is very hard to reach for those turned outward.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "seeker", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation", "general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice"], "original": {"text": "antarmukhasamārādhyā bahirmukhasudurlabhā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "obstacles": ["obs:bahirmukhata"], "concepts": ["cpt:samaya-and-kaula-modes"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:163-164", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "163-164"}, "paraphrase": "She is free of disease, without support, delighting in her own self, a flow of nectar; she is skilled in lifting out those sunk in the mire of saṃsāra.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["karma-liberation"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:169-171", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "169-171"}, "paraphrase": "She abides on both the right-hand and the left-hand paths; she is worshipped by followers of the dakṣiṇa and the non-dakṣiṇa ways; she is Kaulinī and the one who alone grants the priceless state of kaivalya.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "concepts": ["cpt:samaya-and-kaula-modes"], "terms": ["trm:daksinacara", "trm:vamacara", "trm:kaulini"], "disputes": ["dsp:samaya-or-kaula", "dsp:pancamakara-literal-or-substitute"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:177-180", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "177-180"}, "paraphrase": "She is pleased by the worship of suvāsinīs (married women), gratified by the offering into the bindu, the first-born, Tripurāmbikā; worshipped with the ten mudrās, she brings Tripurāśrī under her sway; she is the knowledge-mudrā, reached by knowledge, whose form is knowledge and the known; the yoni-mudrā, lady of the three-part (trikhaṇḍā) mudrā.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["practice"], "concepts": ["cpt:ten-mudras-srividya"], "terms": ["trm:suvasini", "trm:tarpana", "trm:mudra", "trm:trikhanda"], "practices": ["prc:suvasini-puja", "prc:srividya-mudras", "prc:bindu-tarpana"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:182-183", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "182-183"}, "paraphrase": "She dwells in the Śrīcakra, the king of cakras; she is the glorious Tripurasundarī; the auspicious Śivā, whose form is the oneness of Śiva and Śakti, Lalitāmbikā.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "original": {"text": "śrīcakrarājanilayā śrīmattripurasundarī / śrīśivā śivaśaktyaikyarūpiṇī lalitāmbikā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:siva-sakti-union", "cpt:sri-yantra"], "terms": ["trm:sricakra", "trm:tripurasundari"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:2-3", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "2-3"}, "paraphrase": "She bears the noose whose nature is attachment and the goad made of anger; the sugarcane bow is the mind and the five arrows are the five subtle elements (tanmātra); her rosy radiance floods the circle of the universe.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "original": {"text": "rāgasvarūpapāśāḍhyā krodhākārāṅkuśojjvalā / manorūpekṣukodaṇḍā pañcatanmātrasāyakā / nijāruṇaprabhāpūramajjadbrahmāṇḍamaṇḍalā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:lalita-four-weapons"], "terms": ["trm:lalita"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:21-23", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "21-23"}, "paraphrase": "She sits on the lap of Śiva-Kāmeśvara, with her beloved under her sway; she dwells on the central peak of Meru as mistress of Śrīnagara, within the palace of wish-gems (Cintāmaṇi), on the seat of the five Brahmas, in the great lotus-forest and the kadamba grove, in the midst of the ocean of nectar.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:manidvipa-srinagara", "cpt:five-corpse-seat"], "terms": ["trm:sripura", "trm:cintamani-grha", "trm:kamesvara"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:25-33", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "25-33"}, "paraphrase": "The war with Bhaṇḍāsura in names: she rides the Cakrarāja chariot surrounded by hosts of powers; Mantriṇī on the Geyacakra chariot attends her and Daṇḍanāthā (Vārāhī) on the Kiricakra leads the van; Jvālāmālinī raises a wall of fire; Mantriṇī slays Viṣaṅga and Vārāhī slays Viśukra; Gaṇeśa, born of Kāmeśvara's glance, shatters the obstacle-yantra; she destroys Bhaṇḍa and his hosts and revives Kāma burnt by Śiva's eye.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "narrative"], "concepts": ["cpt:lalita-and-bhandasura"], "terms": ["trm:bhandasura", "trm:syamala", "trm:varahi"], "notes": "Verse-range from the local e-text (25-30 checked); the closing name on Kāma's revival placed c. v.33 (not checked).", "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:35-36", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "35-36"}, "paraphrase": "Her lotus face is the Vāgbhava section of the mantra, the part from neck to waist is the middle (Kāmarāja) section, and the part below the waist is the Śakti section; she is the root mantra itself, whose body is the three root sections.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "meditation"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["sound-language", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:three-kutas", "cpt:srividya-mantra-structure"], "terms": ["trm:kuta", "trm:vagbhava-kuta", "trm:kamaraja-kuta", "trm:sakti-kuta", "trm:mula-mantra"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:36-37", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "36-37"}, "paraphrase": "She delights in the nectar of kula and guards the kula conventions; she is the kula-woman, dwells within kula, is Kaulinī and the yoginī of kula; she is also beyond kula (akulā), dwells within Samaya and is intent on Samaya conduct.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "meditation"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["practice", "dispute"], "original": {"text": "kulāṅganā kulāntasthā kaulinī kulayoginī / akulā samayāntasthā samayācāratatparā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:samaya-and-kaula-modes", "cpt:kula-akula"], "terms": ["trm:kula", "trm:akula", "trm:samaya", "trm:samayacara", "trm:kaulini"], "disputes": ["dsp:samaya-or-kaula"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:38-40", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "38-40"}, "paraphrase": "She dwells solely in the mūlādhāra, pierces the knot of Brahmā, rises in the maṇipūra, pierces the knot of Viṣṇu, abides in the ājñā-cakra, pierces the knot of Rudra, mounts the thousand-petalled lotus and showers streams of nectar; she shines like a streak of lightning, abides above the six cakras, is the great power, Kuṇḍalinī, fine as a lotus fibre.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "experiential", "naya": null, "path": ["body-breath", "meditation"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["body-layers", "powers-experiences"], "concepts": ["cpt:kundalini", "cpt:three-granthis", "cpt:cakras"], "terms": ["trm:kundalini", "trm:granthi", "trm:muladhara", "trm:sahasrara"], "paths": ["pth:lalita-kundalini-ascent"], "notes": "The name read 'mahāśaktiḥ' in many editions appears as 'mahāsaktiḥ' in the local stotra e-text; original omitted.", "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:40-42", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "40-42"}, "paraphrase": "She is Bhavānī, reached by contemplation (bhāvanā), the axe for the forest of worldly existence; she loves devotion, is reached by devotion, is won over by devotion, and takes away fear.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["devotion", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "karma-liberation"], "terms": ["trm:bhavana", "trm:bhakti"], "concepts": ["cpt:body-as-sricakra"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:43-45", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "43-45"}, "paraphrase": "She is without support, stainless, untainted, pure, eternal, formless, untroubled, without qualities (nirguṇā), without parts (niṣkalā), peaceful, desireless, indestructible, ever-free, changeless, beyond the world-expanse, without support, ever-pure, ever-awake, faultless, without interval — and the series of such negating names continues.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "apophatic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "original": {"text": "nirlepā nirmalā nityā nirākārā nirākulā / nirguṇā niṣkalā śāntā niṣkāmā nirupaplavā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts (v. 44)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:lalita-as-brahman"], "disputes": ["dsp:saguna-nirguna"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:56-57", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "56-57"}, "paraphrase": "She is worshipped by the sequence of the great sacrifice, honoured by Mahābhairava, witness of the great Lord's great dance at the end of the great aeon; she is the queen of Mahākāmeśa, Mahātripurasundarī.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:tripurasundari", "trm:kamesvara"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:61", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "61"}, "paraphrase": "She is seated on the seat of the five corpses and is of the nature of the five Brahmas; she is made of consciousness, supreme bliss, a mass of knowledge.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "original": {"text": "pañcapretāsanāsīnā pañcabrahmasvarūpiṇī / cinmayī paramānandā vijñānaghanarūpiṇī", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:five-corpse-seat", "cpt:lalita-as-brahman"], "terms": ["trm:pancapretasana"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:62-63", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "62-63"}, "paraphrase": "She is the universal one in waking, Taijasa in dream, Prājña in deep sleep, the fourth (turyā), and she who is devoid of all states.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "meditation"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind"], "original": {"text": "viśvarūpā jāgariṇī svapantī taijasātmikā / suptā prājñātmikā turyā sarvāvasthāvivarjitā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:four-states-and-turya", "cpt:turiya-turiyatita"], "terms": ["trm:turiya", "trm:turiyatita"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:63-64", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "63-64"}, "paraphrase": "She creates in the form of Brahmā, protects in the form of Govinda, withdraws in the form of Rudra, conceals as Īśvarī, grants grace as Sadāśiva, and is devoted to the five acts.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "cosmic", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["world-fate"], "original": {"text": "sṛṣṭikartrī brahmarūpā goptrī govindarūpiṇī / saṃhāriṇī rudrarūpā tirodhānakarīśvarī / sadāśivānugrahadā pañcakṛtyaparāyaṇā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:five-acts-of-the-goddess"], "terms": ["trm:pancakrtya", "trm:tirodhana", "trm:anugraha"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:73", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "73"}, "paraphrase": "She is desirable, and her form is the kāmakalā.", "tags": {"level": "unmarked", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["meditation", "sound"], "stage": "intermediate"}, "types": ["ultimate", "sound-language"], "concepts": ["cpt:kamakala"], "terms": ["trm:kamakala"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:82-83", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "82-83"}, "paraphrase": "She dwells in Jālandhara and in the Oḍyāṇa seat, and in the circle of the bindu; she is worshipped by the sequence of the secret sacrifice (rahoyāga) and gratified by secret libations.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual"], "stage": "advanced"}, "types": ["practice", "body-layers"], "concepts": ["cpt:four-pithas-srividya"], "terms": ["trm:pitha", "trm:rahoyaga", "trm:bindu"], "practices": ["prc:rahoyaga"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:84", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "84"}, "paraphrase": "She is immediately gracious, the witness of the universe, and herself without a witness.", "tags": {"level": "ultimate", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["consciousness-mind", "ultimate"], "terms": ["trm:saksin"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:86-87", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "86-87"}, "paraphrase": "She is unmanifest and of the form of the manifest and the unmanifest; all-pervading, of many forms, of the form of both knowledge and ignorance (vidyā and avidyā); the moonlight that gladdens the lotus of Mahākāmeśa's eyes.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate"], "concepts": ["cpt:maya-as-sakti"], "disputes": ["dsp:maya-sakti-or-avidya"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:89-90", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "89-90"}, "paraphrase": "She is immeasurable, self-luminous, beyond the reach of mind and speech; she is consciousness-power and the form of sentience, and also the power of the insentient and of insentient nature; she is the Gāyatrī, the vyāhṛtis and the twilight prayer, served by the twice-born.", "tags": {"level": "bridging", "standpoint": "analytic", "naya": null, "path": ["knowledge", "ritual"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ultimate", "consciousness-mind"], "original": {"text": "citśaktiś cetanārūpā jaḍaśaktir jaḍātmikā / gāyatrī vyāhṛtiḥ sandhyā dvijavṛndaniṣevitā", "script": "IAST", "edition": "stotra text as in the Nirṇayasāgara ed. with Saubhāgyabhāskara; checked against local e-texts (v. 90)", "licence": "public-domain text; short quotation"}, "concepts": ["cpt:sakti-as-consciousness-power"], "terms": ["trm:cit-sakti", "trm:sakti"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:93", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "93"}, "paraphrase": "She is Kurukullā, ruler of kula, dwells in the kula-pit (at the base), and is served by those devoted to the Kaula path.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ritual", "naya": null, "path": ["ritual", "body-breath"], "stage": "unmarked"}, "types": ["practice"], "terms": ["trm:kula", "trm:kaula"], "disputes": ["dsp:samaya-or-kaula"], "speaker": "the Vāgdevatās (Vaśinī and the others)", "addressee": "Lalitā", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:purvabhaga.32-33", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "purvabhaga.32-33", "section": "pūrvabhāga", "verse": "32-33"}, "paraphrase": "Hayagrīva: commanded by Lalitā, the goddesses of speech composed a supreme hymn of divine secret names; hence it is famed as the 'thousand secret names' (rahasya-nāma-sāhasra).", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "divine", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission", "sound-language"], "speaker": "Hayagrīva", "addressee": "Agastya", "teachers": ["tch:hayagriva", "tch:vagdevatas", "tch:agastya"], "notes": "Numbering of the pūrvabhāga as in the Nirṇayasāgara edition with the Saubhāgyabhāskara (checked).", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "high", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:lalita-sahasranama:uttarabhaga", "source": "src:lalita-sahasranama", "location": {"ref": "uttarabhaga", "section": "uttarabhāga (phalaśruti)"}, "paraphrase": "The concluding section praises the recitation of the thousand names above other rites, lists its fruits, and limits its transmission to devotees of Lalitā.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "devotional", "naya": null, "path": ["sound", "devotion"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["practice", "teacher-transmission"], "speaker": "Hayagrīva", "addressee": "Agastya", "notes": "Summary from memory; verse-level content not checked.", "reported_by_opponent": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": [], "disagreements": []}, "coverage": ["A8"], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "low", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U23-sakta-srividya"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
